Package: raiden-gaming
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @DISTRO_NAME@ <noreply@example.invalid>
Section: games
Priority: optional
Depends: gamemode, procps, kmod, adduser
Recommends: mangohud, gamescope, goverlay
Description: Game tuning for @DISTRO_NAME@
 System settings that make Windows games under Proton and native games run
 faster and smoother, in the spirit of SteamOS and Bazzite:
  - Wine/Proton NT synchronisation in the kernel (ntsync)
  - no split-lock slowdowns on Intel CPUs
  - the memory-map limit SteamOS uses (some games crash with less)
  - larger shader caches for NVIDIA and Mesa (fewer stutters)
  - GameMode set up so it can actually raise CPU speed and game priority
    (Ubuntu leaves out the "gamemode" group its permissions need)
  - Steam listed as "Steam" from the start, on the fast GPU of laptops with
    two graphics chips
